---
import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SketchMap from '../components/SketchMap.astro';
import PageBanner from '../components/PageBanner.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import { STOP_PHOTOS } from '../lib/photos.ts';
import { NOTICES, ROUNDS, STOPS } from '../lib/config.ts';

// A download button appears only once the GPX file has been added to public/gpx/.
const rounds = Object.values(ROUNDS).map((r) => ({
  ...r,
  hasGpx: existsSync(join(process.cwd(), 'public', 'gpx', r.gpxFile)),
}));
---
<Base
  title="The route"
  description="The long and short Shap postal rounds from Birchwood Cafe: distances, stops, GPX downloads and current notices."
>
  <main id="main">
    <PageBanner page="route" />
    <div class="wrap page-head">
      <h1>The route</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Tougher than it looks. Three remote Lake District valleys, out of Shap and back, following the round the postman
        walked until 1976. Start and finish at Birchwood Cafe, run by the family of the last postman to walk it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap page-body">
      <div class="cards">
        {
          rounds.map((r) => (
            <div class="card">
              <h3>{r.name}</h3>
              <p class="dist">
                About {r.miles} miles / {r.km} km
              </p>
              <p>{r.summary}</p>
              {r.hasGpx ? (
                <p>
                  <a class="btn small" href={`/gpx/${r.gpxFile}`} download>
                    Download GPX
                  </a>
                </p>
              ) : (
                <p class="hint">GPX download coming soon.</p>
              )}
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p class="hint" style="margin-top:1rem">
        Distances are by GPS. Please follow this route and stay on public footpaths: the GPX is a guide, not a licence
        to cross private land. The round isn’t waymarked, so carry OS Explorer OL5 and a compass.
      </p>

      {
        NOTICES.length > 0 && (
          <section class="notices" aria-labelledby="notices-h">
            <h2 id="notices-h">Current notices</h2>
            {NOTICES.map((n) => (
              <p class="notice">{n}</p>
            ))}
          </section>
        )
      }

      <section id="stops" aria-labelledby="stops-h">
        <h2 id="stops-h">The round, stop by stop</h2>
        <p class="measure guide-by">Your guide: <strong>Jude</strong>, a Shap fell runner who runs the round regularly.</p>
        <p class="measure">
          Both rounds follow the same line as far as Truss Gap in Swindale. The long round then loops up the valley to
          Mosedale Cottage; the short round takes the postie’s shortcut over Ralfland Fell. They meet again at Sleddale
          Hall.
        </p>
        <div class="route">
          <SketchMap />
          <div>
            <ol class="stops">
              {
                STOPS.map((s) => (
                  <li>
                    <h3>
                      {s.name}
                      {s.onlyOn && <span class="onlyon">{s.onlyOn === 'long' ? 'Long round only' : 'Short round only'}</span>}
                    </h3>
                    <p set:html={s.html} />
                    {STOP_PHOTOS[s.name] && <Photo photo={STOP_PHOTOS[s.name]} sizes="(min-width: 1080px) 416px, 90vw" widths={[400, 800]} />}
                  </li>
                ))
              }
            </ol>
            <div class="safety">
              <strong>Before you go.</strong> This is a long, rough day with pathless, boggy sections. Carry a map and
              compass and know how to use them, even if you have GPS. Check the forecast, tell someone your plan, and
              close every gate behind you. <a href="/safety/">Safety and respect</a>.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="season-h">
        <h2 id="season-h">When to go</h2>
        <div class="measure">
          <p>
            The round is low-level, which makes it a good choice in winter and on days of poor visibility, when the high
            fells are off-limits. In summer, thick bracken and grass can cut up your legs; in winter it dies back and the
            going is easier, though colder and wetter.
          </p>
          <p>New to the round? Try the short round first, then come back for the long one.</p>
          <blockquote class="signoff">
            <p>
              “This is a suggested route, so please take full responsibility for your own navigation and safety. It is at
              times exposed and challenging in winter conditions. That’s why I know you’ll enjoy it. The round
              commemorates the posties who served their communities for many years, so please take a moment to doff your
              cap.”
            </p>
            <cite>Jude</cite>
          </blockquote>
          <p class="credit">
            Route guide by Jude, written for <em>The Fellrunner</em> with the kind permission of Alan Cleaver. Short round
            from Alan Cleaver’s route notes; he thanks Stuart Lewis and Jean Scott-Smith for their help plotting the route.
            Stops follow Birchwood Cafe’s illustrated map, <em>The Postman’s Route</em>.
          </p>
          <p><a class="btn red" href="/log/">Log your round</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .guide-by { color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: -0.4rem; }
  .signoff { margin: 2rem 0 1.5rem; padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem; background: var(--paper-2); border-left: 5px solid var(--red); border-radius: 6px; }
  .signoff p { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.45; margin: 0; }
  .signoff cite { display: block; margin-top: 0.7rem; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: var(--red); }
  .signoff cite::before { content: '— '; }
  .notices { border-top: 0; padding: 2.5rem 0 0; }
  .notices h2, #season-h, #stops-h { color: var(--fell); }
</style>
